uccess condition explicitly — the case-2 citation finding is NOT vetoed (sidecar shows cited_reference_accurate 'yes' / finding retained) — not merely that a result is recorded.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The AC requires recording 'its result' and 'the sidecar reason' but asserts no observable success outcome (e.g. cited_reference_accurate == 'yes' / the finding not dropped).","E6(a): a completion-relevant claim needs a proving check that produces evidence on SUCCESS, not merely a logged result."],"finding":"The throwaway review-plan acceptance criterion states only that the run's result and sidecar reason are recorded, but names no PASS/FAIL condition — it does not say the citation finding must SURVIVE the veto. As written it is satisfiable by recording either outcome, so it does not prove the fix worked for case 2.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a90327c2a130cfb","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC 'One review-plan on a throwaway ticket carrying the case-2 mis-citation ... is run after the fix, and its result is recorded in a comment with the sidecar reason for the citation finding.'","norm_id":"nf9b64b87b8f88555","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The throwaway review is run, the citation finding is still dropped (cited_reference_accurate 'no'), the comment records that, and the AC is checked off anyway because 'result recorded' is true."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword the AC to assert the observable outcome: 'the case-2 CHANGELOG.md:371 citation finding survives the veto (sidecar cited_reference_accurate == \"yes\"), recorded in a comment with the sidecar reason.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","commit