advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'by majority of 3 runs (measured margin: 3/3 on the fixed prompts for both variants; 0/3 agentic and 1/3 single-turn on the unfixed prompts)'","docs/plan-review-gate.md plan-v5: 'Ordinal severity labels are an LLM anti-pattern: models do not apply none|low|medium|high reliably enough for deterministic gate behavior'","The veto is deterministic in decide.py:635 but its only input (cited_reference_accurate) is set by the LLM verifier, so correctness now rests on prompt adherence with no location check","The single-turn unfixed baseline already answers the plan-citation case correctly 1/3 of the time, so the fixed-vs-unfixed separation for that arm is 1/3→3/3 at n=3"],"finding":"The fix is a pure prompt-wording scoping change verified only by a majority of 3 live samples per arm on an instruction-following surface the gate's own docs characterize as unreliable (plan-v5: 'ordinal severity labels are an LLM anti-pattern; models do not apply them reliably enough for deterministic gate behavior'); the recorded single-turn margin is thin (unfixed already 1/3, fixed 3/3), so prompt drift or verifier-model variance could silently reopen the defect on a blocking-tier criterion (G6 0.60 / E4 0.75) with no deterministic guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f74b7c5a552e8ba71","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1-2 + Acceptance Criteria (live-test pass/fail bullets)","norm_id":"ne8cfef134559a227","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future verifier-model swap or a prompt edit elsewhere in the shared prefix re-destabilizes the single-turn arm and correct plan-citation findings silently drop again","A real throwaway/field plan with a wrong plan-citation finding lands just under the 2/3 majority on a bad sampling day and the finding is vetoed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absen